# Theravāda Research Corpus

## Purpose

Structured research corpus for the study of Theravāda Buddhism,
Pāli Canon, Theravāda philosophy, Abhidhamma, meditation
and classical commentarial traditions.

## Primary Canonical Corpus

Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana Tipiṭaka (CST)

Primary source:
Vipassana Research Institute / Tipitaka.org

Repository source:
VipassanaTech/tipitaka-xml

Working script:
Roman Pāli

## Research hierarchy

1. Pāli Canon — Mūla
2. Aṭṭhakathā — Commentaries
3. Ṭīkā — Subcommentaries
4. Classical systematic texts
5. Pāli philology and dictionaries
6. Academic Buddhist Studies
7. Modern Theravāda traditions
8. Comparative analysis

## Source policy

Canonical text, commentary, subcommentary,
modern Theravāda interpretation and academic reconstruction
must remain explicitly distinguished.
